30,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Kenji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... I've looked at the records. I'm a bit worried. The suspended bay has a strict weight limit, and the powered displays have been breaking down a lot lately. We should be very careful about what we choose.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The data suggests a clear pattern. Visitors are drawn to dynamic displays and human interaction. Static exhibits are less effective at encouraging repeat visits, which is a critical metric for our success.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,"Oh no! It's even worse than I thought! The conservation lab is almost empty, and there's a huge mountain of stuff waiting to be fixed. We can't pick anything that needs a lot of cleaning or special care!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"I've got some bad news too! It looks like we've had a lot of trouble with shipping deadlines lately, and the costs for moving art are way higher than I expected. We really need to be careful!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we are facing a perfect storm of constraints. I've discovered that bespoke mounting costs are skyrocketing, and our evening hires leave the gallery vulnerable to accidental damage. We must avoid anything requiring custom carpentry or fragile layouts.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Rin, @Kenji... it sounds like everything is really struggling. If the lab is full and shipping is hard, maybe we should avoid anything heavy or high-tech? I'm scared the floor might not hold something too big.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, while I understand your caution, we must not overcorrect. If we choose something too simple, we risk a failure in engagement. The records show that static displays simply do not bring people back.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, but if we pick something ""dynamic"" and it breaks or needs fixing, there's only one person in the lab! We can't just ignore the people doing the work! They'll be super stressed!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin is right! And if we pick something with tons of loans from far away, we might not even have the art here on opening day. We need a plan that's actually possible to pull off!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, while engagement is a noble goal, it is a luxury we cannot afford if the cost is a financial or structural collapse. Logic suggests we prioritize stability over spectacle this season.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree with Benjamin. If the bay is already struggling and the powered displays keep failing, a ""dynamic"" show might just mean more broken things and roped-off areas. We can't risk the building's safety.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, @Benjamin, safety is paramount, but a gallery that no one visits is equally useless. We must find a balance where human presence or simple movement provides the engagement without overloading the infrastructure.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, but ""human presence"" means more work for the staff! If the volunteers are mostly just town historians, they can't do everything. We need a show that doesn't make the few people we have collapse!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"Exactly! We can't just hope for the best. If we pick a show with too many complicated loans, we'll just be apologizing to everyone at the door again. Let's keep it simple and reliable!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, @Rin, your concerns are quite valid. If we combine skyrocketing carpentry costs with a depleted lab and shipping chaos, a complex exhibition becomes a liability. We should seek a proposal that is self-contained and low-maintenance.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I just don't want anyone to get hurt or for the gallery to be damaged. Please, let's choose the option that is the lightest and simplest for the building to handle.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"I understand the risks, but we must not forget the visitor. A sterile, empty gallery is a failure of a different kind. Let us look for a candidate that balances stability with genuine human engagement.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,I just want everyone to be happy and not too tired! Let's pick a show that doesn't need a million people to run it or a huge team to fix it. Simple is best!,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I'm with you, Rin! Let's avoid anything that relies on a bunch of risky shipments from far away. If we pick something reliable, we can actually enjoy the show instead of worrying about the mail!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we have reached a consensus on the necessity of caution. Let us evaluate the candidates through this lens: minimal custom construction, low staffing demands, and structural modesty. Elegance, after all, often lies in simplicity.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
