60,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... looking at these, Option D seems really scary because of the rigging and the powered displays. Option C has a working bench, which might be too much for the lab. Maybe Option A is the safest?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, I agree that Option D is too risky. However, Option A is ideal. The demonstration sessions provide the human interaction and dynamism that the data shows visitors crave, without stressing the infrastructure.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, I love the idea of craftspeople coming in! That means the experts do the work, not the tired staff in the lab. Option A is perfect because it's local and simple!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Kenji,,I totally agree! Option A is the best because it's local. No scary shipping delays or huge transport costs from far away. We can actually be sure everything will be here on time!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option A is indeed the most logical choice. It avoids the exorbitant costs of bespoke mounting and the risks of shipping, while its simplicity protects the gallery from the hazards of our evening hires.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I feel much better now that we all agree. Option A is light, it doesn't need complex rigging, and it won't hurt the floor. I think it's the only one that's truly safe for the building.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,It is rare that our various constraints align so perfectly with the needs of the public. Option A satisfies the requirement for engagement while remaining practically viable. I am fully in favor of this selection.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,"And it's the kindest choice for the staff! Since the craftspeople help out, the one person in the lab can finally breathe. I'm voting for Option A! It's a win-win for everyone!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Kenji,,Me too! Option A is the only one that doesn't make me nervous about the delivery trucks. Let's go with the local textiles so we can have a stress-free opening day! I'm voting for A!,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,It is a rare pleasure when the most prudent financial decision also happens to be the most aesthetically and socially sound. Option A is the only choice that doesn't invite a budgetary disaster. I vote for A.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I'm glad we could find something that works for everyone. I feel much more confident now. I'll vote for Option A too.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,The consensus is absolute. Option A provides the human element necessary for repeat visits without compromising our fragile infrastructure or exhausted staff. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,Yay! Everyone is happy and the staff can take a nap! I'm so glad we picked the one that's easy and fun. Option A all the way! I vote for A!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm so happy we all agree! No more worrying about missing crates or late paperwork. Let's make this the smoothest opening the museum has ever had! I vote for Option A!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Since we have achieved a rare and complete unanimity, there is little left to debate. Option A is the only candidate that respects both our budget and our sanity. I cast my final vote for A.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I'm just... really relieved. Thank you for understanding my worries about the building. I'm happy we can have a beautiful show that is safe for everyone. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"The decision is sound. By prioritizing the human element through local craftspeople, we ensure the exhibition's success without risking the museum's stability. I cast my vote for Option A.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Rin,,I'm so happy we're all on the same page! Let's make it a great show that doesn't make anyone cry from being too tired! I vote for Option A!,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"I'm so glad we're doing this! It's going to be an awesome exhibition, and the best part is that we can actually relax knowing everything is local. I vote for Option A!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,A most satisfactory conclusion. We have successfully navigated the treacherous waters of our budget and infrastructure to find a solution that is as sustainable as it is engaging. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
